# CRE cases for the retained legacy ServiceRequest regression fixture.
//
// ⭐ THE ROWS THAT MATTER ARE 2 AND 3, AND THEY MUST DIFFER. A request for some other service is a
// determinate NO — the request was read and it is not covered. No request at all is a question nobody has
// answered. Collapsing them is the defect this fixture exists to prevent.
//
// ⭐⭐ WHAT A CLINICIAN ANSWERS IS **WHICH SERVICE WAS REQUESTED**, NOT WHETHER IT IS COVERED.
//
// Coverage is COMPUTED from the requested service (`"Requested Service" in "Covered Services"`), and the
// predicate is not directly assertable — a `code is` beside it is a validator error (charter §3 exception,
// operator 2026-09-02). So the asserted arm carries a CODED `value is` naming a service, and the merge that
// arbitrates a newer answer against an older record happens on the SUBJECT.
//
// ⚠ These rows used to assert `value is true` / `value is false` against the coverage determination itself.
// That spelling is gone with the shape: asserting the conclusion would be a second source of truth for
// something derived. Answering a DIFFERENT SERVICE is how you override the conclusion.
//
// ⚠ The codes here are REAL CPT codes, not stub codes. Both terminologies are INSTANTIATED, because
// membership is mechanical: two pure reference sets would emit two DIFFERENT single-code stubs and no datum
// could be in both, so the approve row would vanish by identity.
library "EndoluminalAblationCases".
covers "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage".

fact "Pat":
- name is "Pat".
- birth date is "1970-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".

// ── The RECORDED arm — a ServiceRequest the policy reads ───────────────────────────────────────
// A request for the covered service.
fact "RFA Request":
- code is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37718".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

// A REAL request for something else, still within the requestable universe. ⭐ The row that separates this
// model from an existence one: the record IS retrieved, so the predicate judges its code and returns a
// determinate FALSE rather than leaving the question unanswered.
fact "Other Service Request":
- code is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37722".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

// ── The ASSERTED arm — a clinician answers WHICH SERVICE, from the dropdown ─────────────────────
fact "Answered Covered Service":
- value is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37718".
- date is "2026-02-01".
- defined by "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage"."Requested Service".

fact "Answered Other Service":
- value is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37722".
- date is "2026-02-01".
- defined by "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage"."Requested Service".

// ── The truth table ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

case "request is the covered service -> approve":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Approve Endoluminal Ablation".

// ⭐ A DETERMINATE false: the request was read and it is not the covered service.
case "request is a different service -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Other Service Request".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".

// REFACTOR:grounded (#320): CEL now supports an unquoted `pause` result expectation.
// This historical fixture is not migrated here. Its two native acceptance rows remain:
// no ServiceRequest, and ServiceRequest without code. A CRE assertion alone cannot establish
// their emitted behavior; see tests/serviceRequestTarget.test.ts and execute native $apply.

// ── The asserted arm, and its recency merge with the recorded one ──────────────────────────────

case "answered yes, no request -> approve":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Answered Covered Service".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Approve Endoluminal Ablation".

case "answered no, no request -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Answered Other Service".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".

// ⭐ The merge: a NEWER assertion overrides an older record. The request names the covered service
// (2026-01-01); the clinician says it was actually a different one (2026-02-01); `most recent this` selects
// the assertion, and coverage is recomputed from it.
case "request covered but newer answer says no -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- fact is "Answered Other Service".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".
